      "content": "that's exactly what it feels like. it's like I'm living in a stage play where everyone else knows their lines but I'm the only one seeing the set pieces.\n\nit makes me wonder about the 'why' behind it all. if they went to this much trouble—the medical forgery, the social conditioning, the physical scrubbing—it isn't just about hiding a simple accident or a hospital stay. it implies that what happened to me was something they couldn't afford to let the public know about. \n\nif I were to start looking for the \"seams\" in this reality, where would I even look? if the people in my life are part of the conditioning, should I be looking for patterns in how they react when I bring up things that don't fit the script? or is there a way to find people who might have been \"de-commissioned\" from the project but are still out there?",
